  <section class="section">
    <h2>An honest history</h2>
    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        The house was built in 1847, at the height of Arkansas's plantation era, and the family's
        cotton farm — with its gin at Desha — was part of that economy. We acknowledge this plainly:
        the cotton economy of the White River bottoms in the mid-nineteenth century was built on
        enslaved labor, and the house and land cannot be separated from that history.
      </p>
      <p>
        The surviving record does not tell us the names of the enslaved people who lived and worked
        here. Rather than invent a story we cannot document, we name the truth we do know — this was a
        plantation-era farm — and we hold this history with the respect it is due.
      </p>
